Menu="User Utilities"
Title="npm-auto"
Icon="random"
---
<?php
require_once "$docroot/plugins/npm-auto/include/common.php";

$cfg     = npm_auto_cfg();
$lan_ip  = npm_auto_lan_ip();
$running = npm_auto_running();
$status  = npm_auto_status();
$managed = npm_auto_read_json(NPM_AUTO_MANAGED) ?? [];
$pass_saved = ($cfg['NPM_PASS'] ?? '') !== '';

// One line a person can act on: is it on, and is NPM answering?
if (($cfg['SERVICE'] ?? '') !== 'enable') {
    $status_line = _('Disabled');
} elseif (!$running) {
    $status_line = _('Stopped') . ' - ' . _('starts with the array');
} elseif (!$status) {
    $status_line = _('Starting');
} elseif (($status['npm'] ?? '') !== 'ok') {
    $status_line = _('Running') . ' - ' . _('NPM') . ': ' . ($status['error'] ?? _('not reachable'));
} else {
    $status_line = _('Running') . ' - ' . sprintf(_('%d managed proxy hosts'), count($managed))
        . ', ' . _('last checked') . ' ' . date('H:i:s', (int)($status['time'] ?? 0));
}
?>
<form markdown="1" name="npm_auto_settings" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="npm-auto/npm-auto.cfg">
<input type="hidden" name="#include" value="plugins/npm-auto/include/update.php">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/plugins/npm-auto/scripts/rc.npm-auto">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="apply">

_(Status)_:
: <?=htmlspecialchars($status_line)?>

_(Enable npm-auto)_:
: <select name="SERVICE">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['SERVICE'], 'disable', _('No'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['SERVICE'], 'enable', _('Yes'))?>
  </select>

> Runs the background service that keeps Nginx Proxy Manager in step with the **Auto Proxy** switches on the Docker tab.
> Disabling it stops the service and leaves every NPM entry as it is; use the cleanup below first to remove them.

_(NPM host)_:
: <input type="text" name="NPM_HOST" class="narrow" maxlength="253" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['NPM_HOST'])?>" placeholder="<?=htmlspecialchars($lan_ip)?>" pattern="[A-Za-z0-9.:\-]*">

_(NPM admin port)_:
: <input type="number" name="NPM_PORT" class="narrow" min="1" max="65535" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['NPM_PORT'])?>" placeholder="81">

> Where the Nginx Proxy Manager admin interface answers. Leave the host blank to use this server's own address (<?=htmlspecialchars($lan_ip ?: _('not detected'))?>), which is right when NPM runs as a container here.

_(NPM user)_:
: <input type="text" name="NPM_USER" maxlength="200" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['NPM_USER'])?>" autocomplete="off" placeholder="admin@example.com">

_(NPM password)_:
: <input type="password" name="NPM_PASS" maxlength="200" value="" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="<?=$pass_saved ? _('Saved - leave blank to keep') : ''?>">

> An NPM account allowed to manage proxy hosts. The password is stored in npm-auto.cfg on the flash drive and is never sent back to the browser.

_(Default domain)_:
: <input type="text" name="DEFAULT_DOMAIN" maxlength="200" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['DEFAULT_DOMAIN'])?>" placeholder="example.com" pattern="[A-Za-z0-9.\-]*">

> Each proxied container is served at *container-name*.*default-domain* unless an override says otherwise.
> Point a wildcard DNS record for this domain at NPM.

_(Use container labels)_:
: <select name="LABEL_OVERRIDES">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['LABEL_OVERRIDES'], 'yes', _('Yes'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['LABEL_OVERRIDES'], 'no', _('No'))?>
  </select>

> Lets a container choose its own name and port with Docker labels (add them under Extra Parameters):
> `npm-auto.domain` sets the full domain, e.g. `-l npm-auto.domain=media.example.com`;
> `npm-auto.port` sets the host port NPM forwards to, e.g. `-l npm-auto.port=8181`.
> Without a port label, npm-auto uses the port in the container's WebUI setting, then its lowest published port.

_(Attach SSL certificates)_:
: <select name="AUTO_SSL">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['AUTO_SSL'], 'yes', _('Yes'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['AUTO_SSL'], 'no', _('No'))?>
  </select>

> Uses an unexpired certificate already in NPM that covers the name (exact or wildcard) and forces HTTPS.
> npm-auto never requests certificates.

_(When Auto Proxy is switched off)_:
: <select name="TOGGLE_OFF_ACTION">
  <?=mk_option($cfg['TOGGLE_OFF_ACTION'], 'keep', _('Keep the NPM entry and stop managing it'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['TOGGLE_OFF_ACTION'], 'disable', _('Disable the NPM entry (reversible)'))?>
  <?=mk_option($cfg['TOGGLE_OFF_ACTION'], 'delete', _('Delete the NPM entry'))?>
  </select>

> Also applies when a proxied container is removed.

&nbsp;
: <input type="submit" name="#apply" value="_(Apply)_"><input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</form>

<div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-random title"></i>_(Docker tab)_</span></div>

The Docker tab gains two columns: **Auto Proxy**, a switch per container, and **Subdomain**, the name it is (or will be) served at.
Click a subdomain to choose a different one; a live entry is renamed within about 15 seconds, with no container restart.
Clear it to go back to the default. An override set there takes priority over the `npm-auto.domain` label.
Proxy hosts made by hand in NPM are shown too, muted, but npm-auto does not change them.

<div class="title"><span class="left"><i class="fa fa-wrench title"></i>_(Managed proxy hosts)_</span></div>

Apply an action now to every proxy host npm-auto manages (<?=count($managed)?>). Uninstalling the plugin never touches NPM, so run a cleanup first if you want one.

<input type="button" id="npm-auto-cleanup-disable" value="_(Disable all)_">
<input type="button" id="npm-auto-cleanup-delete" value="_(Delete all)_">
<input type="button" value="_(View log)_" onclick="openTerminal('log','npm-auto','npm-auto.log')">
<span id="npm-auto-cleanup-status"></span>

<script>
$(function() {
  function requestCleanup(mode, text) {
    swal({title: "_(npm-auto)_", text: text, type: 'warning', showCancelButton: true,
          confirmButtonText: "_(Proceed)_", cancelButtonText: "_(Cancel)_"}, function() {
      $.post('/plugins/npm-auto/webGui/settings.php', {action: 'cleanup', mode: mode, csrf_token: csrf_token}, null, 'json')
        .done(function(data) {
          $('#npm-auto-cleanup-status').text(data.ok
            ? "_(Requested - applied within about 15 seconds)_"
            : data.error);
        })
        .fail(function() { $('#npm-auto-cleanup-status').text("_(Request failed)_"); });
    });
  }
  $('#npm-auto-cleanup-disable').click(function() {
    requestCleanup('disable', "_(Disable every proxy host npm-auto manages?)_");
  });
  $('#npm-auto-cleanup-delete').click(function() {
    requestCleanup('delete', "_(Delete every proxy host npm-auto manages, created and adopted alike?)_");
  });
});
</script>
